Theorem RL-comp: whole-suite evaluator behavior, exact trace, and projection satisfaction

  Preconditions:
    - Every active RL constituent discharges, including RL-11a/14a/15a/18a,
      the RL-13 removal confirmation, and RL-1/RL-2 multi-use composition.
    - Canonical evaluator behavior is the semantic oracle.
    - AllocationFacts freezes an exact AIMS logical trace.
    - A physical plan is admitted only through the separate Satisfies relation.

  Soundness property:
    Forall realized function F and admitted projection P:
      (P1) evaluator_behavior(realize(F)) = evaluator_behavior(F).
      (P2) projection_trace(P) = aimsTrace(facts(F)) exactly, including
           OwnershipObservationFacts and CleanupObligation identities.
      (P3) Satisfies(facts(F), extent(F), capabilities(P)).
      (P4) RL-comp is exactly as strong as the conjunction of all constituents.
    Behavior parity, trace equality, and Satisfies are independent obligations;
    no physical ARC/reference-counter baseline is used as a semantic oracle.

  Proof obligation:
    - Re-run all 38 active RL constituent verifiers and require Valid.
    - Re-run the RL-1/RL-2 combined multi-use obligation.
    - Compare canonical and realized evaluator behavior on aliased and
      unaliased mutation cases.
    - Compare the capability trace directly with the exact AIMS trace.
    - Check Satisfies separately even when trace equality holds.
    - Coverage gate: exactly 38 constituents; none may be dropped.

    Negative-direction witnesses:
      A shared same-identity mutation changes an alias view and fails behavior
      parity. A changed observation identity fails exact trace equality. A plan
      with insufficient owner capacity fails Satisfies.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl_composition)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-comp composes 38 constituents with independent canonical evaluator behavior, exact AIMS logical trace equality, and Satisfies obligations
